-- title:
--   Supersingular node pairs are stable under diamond operators
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic a prime $p$, let $N \ge 1$, assume $p \nmid N$, and let $H' \le (\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$. Write $F =$ `qExpFunctionFieldC K (CohCarrier.GammaH N H')` for the $K$-subfield of the Laurent series over $K$ generated by the ratios $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_f/\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_g$ of reductions of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight for the subgroup $\Gamma_{H'}(N) \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ attached to $H'$, and let places of $F$ over $K$ be the proper valuation subrings of $F$ containing $K$ whose valuation ring is a principal ideal ring. Let $T$ be a finite set of pairs of such places, and assume that a pair $s$ lies in $T$ if and only if $s$ lies in `ssNodePairsQExp K (CohCarrier.GammaH N H') p`, that is, $s_2$ is a supersingular place (`IsSSPlaceQExp`) and $s_1 =$ `qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL K (CohCarrier.GammaH N H') p s_2`, the restriction of $s_2$ along the characteristic-$p$ Frobenius endomorphism of $F$. Then for every unit $e$ of $\mathbb{Z}/N$ the set $T$ is node-stable for the semilinear automorphism obtained from the $K$-algebra automorphism `diamondActionModL K N H' (CuspForm.gammaLift N e)` of $F$ paired with the identity of $K$: for every $s \in T$ the pair $(g \cdot s_1, g \cdot s_2)$ again lies in $T$. Here `diamondActionModL` is the chosen homomorphism $\Gamma_0(N) \to \mathrm{Aut}_K(F)$ satisfying `IsDiamondPullbackModL` (and trivial if none exists), evaluated at a chosen lift of $e$ to $\Gamma_0(N)$ under the determinant-type map `gamma0Units`.
--
--   This is the statement that the diamond operator $\langle e \rangle$ permutes the supersingular node pairs $(\mathrm{Frob}\,y, y)$ on the characteristic-$p$ fibre of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_{H'}(N)$, in the function-field formulation used in the project. It serves as the node-stability input for the construction of the diamond action on the special fibre and on the associated glued degree-zero Picard functor, and is used in the analysis of the Hecke and Frobenius relations on the Néron model at $p$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_isNodeStable_ofAlgAut_diamondActionModL_of_forall_mem_iff_mem_ssNodePairsQExp_of_not_dvd.lean

